      <item>
       <widget class="LocationTemplatePatternsEditor" name="templates_editor">
        <property name="toolTip">
         <string>Each row is a path template: the Locations grammar, with / between folder levels. Double-click a cell to edit it.</string>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
      <item>
       <widget class="WrappingLabel" name="templates_note_label">
        <property name="text">
         <string>The root editor's Path template drop-down offers these, after *, for each type that accepts them. A template uses the Locations placeholders {title}, {publisher}, {authors} and {year}, plus {count} for a type that declares it, with {{ ... }} groups that drop out when a field inside is empty, and / between folder levels: {authors}/{title}{{ [{year}]}}. A template that does not parse, or names an unknown placeholder, is kept and shown in red, and not offered; so is a * row, which the drop-down always has. A root keeps the template it was given: editing this list changes no root.</string>
        </property>
        <property name="wordWrap">
         <bool>true</bool>
        </property>
       </widget>
      </item>
     </layout>
    </widget>
